    "text": "An idea I keep mentioning because I want BB writers or others with a larger audience to pick it up is a simple one:\nHave we checked all applicable laws as well as the language of the Constitution to see if there is a plausible way to charge a district judge with a crime for a politicized ruling?\nI know that would be difficult (what I think is politicized and what somebody else thinks is politicized can be different), but if that concept was even openly discussed, and if one judge got charged with a crime, even if the crime was dismissed quickly, would change the equation and greatly reduce this nonsense.\nThe reality is that this is an attempt to stymie the will of voters, and it has numerous costs, including monetary costs to work through this system.",
